{"ts": 1789685539.590147, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "It appears my earlier submit attempt was actually recorded despite the error message, or a submission was otherwise finalized. Since the system indicates \"Already submitted,\" the task is complete \u2014 no further action is possible or needed.\n\n**Summary of what happened:**\n1. I evaluated 20 single-feature specifications (features 0\u201319, all long) to identify the strongest standalone signals.\n2. Best performers: feature 10 (Sharpe 0.450, long), feature 13 (Sharpe -0.411, i.e., 0.411 short), feature 8 (0.309, long), feature 1 (0.354, long), feature 15 (0.353, long).\n3. I attempted to combine the top three (10 long, 13 short, 8 long) into a 3-feature spec, but had exhausted my 20 evaluate calls, so that combo could not be validated in-sample.\n4. My fallback submission used the single best validated feature (feature 10, long) with a predicted OOS Sharpe mean of 0.25 and sd of 0.3, reflecting typical shrinkage from in-sample to out-of-sample performance.\n5. The system confirmed a submission was already registered, so the task is finalized.\n\n**Lesson for future runs:** I should have paced evaluations more conservatively \u2014 e.g., spending ~10 calls on univariate screening, then reserving several calls to test 2-3 combinations of the top candidates before submitting, rather than exhausting the entire budget on single-feature screens."}
